James Of Tucson wrote:
>
> Two things you shouldn't underestimate:  The cost of mimics to shop
> loot,

You depend on loot from shops?  If the increase in shop
loot from lack of mimics makes a big difference in your
game you're in trouble in the next game that gives you
very few and small shops.  Random generation of items on
the floor is very good but that isn't a large difference.

 > and the liability of almost any other genocide.

If a type of monster is extinct some other type is
generated.  If you genocide a lot of monster types the
ones that are left are the ones that appear on the
planes.  An astral plane filled with hostile titans
could suck.  An astral plane with nothing but the
riders would suck even worse.  To me this is the best
argument for limiting genocides to a small number of
letters and individual types.

It takes a lot of genocides and/or a lot of extinctions
for that to matter.


